WEBVTT

00:00:07.779 --> 00:00:10.691
Build a room notice that keeps its information

00:00:10.691 --> 00:00:13.097
readable when the window changes size.

00:00:13.097 --> 00:00:16.517
We will arrange its title, room and instructions, then

00:00:16.517 --> 00:00:19.429
test the real window in the Workspace Desktop.

00:00:47.190 --> 00:00:51.007
A VBox arranges children vertically; an HBox arranges

00:00:51.007 --> 00:00:52.304
them horizontally.

00:00:52.304 --> 00:00:54.897
Spacing separates adjacent children.

00:00:54.897 --> 00:00:58.642
Padding, supplied by Insets, leaves space inside the

00:00:58.642 --> 00:01:00.154
container's boundary.

00:01:00.154 --> 00:01:03.611
The title's inline style is a Java String of CSS

00:01:03.611 --> 00:01:07.429
presentation declarations: each property has a colon,

00:01:07.429 --> 00:01:08.869
value and semicolon.

00:01:08.869 --> 00:01:11.390
Here they set font size and weight.

00:01:11.695 --> 00:01:14.863
The scene requests a content area of four hundred

00:01:14.863 --> 00:01:16.674
forty by two hundred twenty.

00:01:16.674 --> 00:01:19.648
Window borders and the title bar are separate.

00:01:19.648 --> 00:01:21.588
Predict the two console lines.

00:01:21.588 --> 00:01:24.691
When we narrow this window, will the note's line

00:01:24.691 --> 00:01:26.696
breaks stay in the same places?

00:01:26.696 --> 00:01:27.795
Pause and decide.

00:01:41.965 --> 00:01:45.205
The console reports Lab A and wrapping enabled.

00:01:45.205 --> 00:01:48.721
In the notice, the horizontal room row sits between

00:01:48.721 --> 00:01:50.582
the title and instructions.

00:01:50.582 --> 00:01:54.305
Wrapping allows long text to use multiple lines within

00:01:54.305 --> 00:01:55.683
its available width.

00:01:55.683 --> 00:01:59.268
The title's larger, bold text marks its role without

00:01:59.268 --> 00:02:00.440
relying on color.

00:02:04.482 --> 00:02:06.619
The native window is now narrower.

00:02:06.619 --> 00:02:09.951
The containers recalculate their layout, and the note

00:02:09.951 --> 00:02:11.585
breaks at different words.

00:02:11.585 --> 00:02:13.911
Its full instruction remains visible.

00:02:13.911 --> 00:02:17.117
Spacing still separates the sections, while padding

00:02:17.117 --> 00:02:19.632
keeps their content away from the edges.

00:02:19.632 --> 00:02:22.775
Resizing changes the view; it does not print a new

00:02:22.775 --> 00:02:24.032
construction report.

00:02:28.282 --> 00:02:31.643
If this notice moved to another room, which text would

00:02:31.643 --> 00:02:34.320
you change, and how would you test that the

00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:37.432
instructions remain readable in a narrower window?
